<body>
<p>Reports request-matcher registrations (<code>requestMatchers</code>, <code>mvcMatchers</code>,
  <code>antMatchers</code>, <code>regexMatchers</code>) that are chained <b>after</b> <code>anyRequest()</code>
  inside an <code>authorizeHttpRequests</code> / <code>authorizeRequests</code> block.</p>

<p><code>anyRequest()</code> must be the last matcher in the authorization chain. Configuring another matcher after it
  makes Spring Security fail at startup with <code>Can't configure requestMatchers after anyRequest</code>.</p>

<p><b>Incorrect:</b></p>
<pre><code>
  http.authorizeHttpRequests(auth -> auth
    .requestMatchers("/", "/home").permitAll()
    .anyRequest().authenticated()
    .requestMatchers("/admin/**").hasRole("ADMIN")   // reports: configured after anyRequest()
  );
</code></pre>

<p><b>Correct</b> (move <code>anyRequest()</code> to the end):</p>
<pre><code>
  http.authorizeHttpRequests(auth -> auth
    .requestMatchers("/", "/home").permitAll()
    .requestMatchers("/admin/**").hasRole("ADMIN")
    .anyRequest().authenticated()
  );
</code></pre>
</body>
</html>
